# Ten summon-and-kill blocks. (bd inc-q98a)
#
# Not a session of its own. It exists so that the two scripts that need
# multiples of ten -- tools/keys/monster-memory-kills.keys, which wants ten,
# and tools/keys/monster-memory-saturate.keys, which wants two hundred and
# sixty -- say how many they want instead of carrying that many copies of the
# block. tools/keys/monster-memory-one-kill.keys is the block itself and
# explains why it is shaped as it is.

